ase</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1997</year><volume>275</volume><fpage>1308</fpage><lpage>1311</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9036856</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Andr&#x000e9;oli</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Le-Borgne</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Reggio</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Mangeat</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ezrin has properties to self-associate at the plasma membrane</article-title><source>J Cell Sci</source><year>1994</year><volume>107</volume><fpage>2509</fpage><lpage>2521</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7844168</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Araki</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kikuchi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hata</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Isomura</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Takai</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regulation of reversible binding of smg p25A, a ras p21-like GTP-binding protein, to synaptic plasma membranes and vesicles by its specific regulatory protein, GDP-dissociation inhibitor</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1990</year><volume>265</volume><fpage>13007</fpage><lpage>13015</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2115887</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Arpin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Algrain</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Louvard</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><artic